A||||2||Seanh||How do I remove the Dash?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||08-18-2000||04:39 PM||||I am wanting to re-paint my dash this weekend and I looked all through the Haynes Manual and it doesent say exacly how to remove it. I heard its kinda difficult but it needs to get done. Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Currently upgrading to a NorthStar.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-18-2000||10:26 PM||||Easy... unbolt EVERYTHING and it comes right out. Seriously, You have to remove the control pod, which means you have to remove the shifter surround. Then you have to remove the gauge pod. The dash is held in with two screws hidden under the speaker grills and one bolt on the bottom corners under each vent.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||2
Z||000002||theogre||08-18-2000||10:41 PM||||This is more of a 3 day project if you've never done it. It will take time to tear it down pluss you have to clean everything proper or the paint will look like hell.<P>In addition to the radio suround slash control pod, you also have to strip the entire speedometer area from above the steering column. It's not hard but quite a time killer.<P>Once you have the 6 actual dash screws and bolts out....<P>there are also 2 tabs on the "pod" frame that tie into the opening for the middle air duct. Carefully pull out on the pod frame and the tabs should clear as you lift the dash out. Be gentle or the frame may break. ||||reg||1
